---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
---
<Base title="Annuities" description="Annuities explained in plain words by a local agent in McKees Rocks, PA. What they are, what they are not, and when they make sense.">
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Annuities"
    title="Turn part of your savings into a steady check."
    intro="An annuity is a contract with an insurance company. You give it a sum of money, and it pays you back over time, often for life. It is not right for everyone, and I will tell you if it is not right for you."
    photo="paperwork"
  />

  <Prose heading="When people ask about one." eyebrow="Common reasons">
    <ul>
      <li>You want income you cannot outlive, on top of Social Security or a pension.</li>
      <li>You want part of your savings protected from market drops.</li>
      <li>A CD is coming due and you want to compare your choices.</li>
    </ul>
  </Prose>

  <Prose heading="What to know first." eyebrow="Straight talk" tone="sage">
    <p>Most annuities tie up your money for a set number of years. Taking it out early usually means a surrender charge. Keep enough in savings for emergencies before you put anything into an annuity.</p>
    <p>I walk you through the surrender period, the fees and how the payments work, in writing, before you sign anything. Take the papers home. Show your kids or your accountant.</p>
  </Prose>

  <Prose heading="What to bring." eyebrow="How I help">
    <ul>
      <li>A rough idea of your monthly income and expenses.</li>
      <li>Statements for any savings or CDs you are thinking about using.</li>
      <li>Your questions. All of them.</li>
    </ul>
  </Prose>
</Base>
